1. 3D object scans: Google Scanned Objects (CC BY 4.0)

This project uses 3D models from Google Scanned Objects (Google Research; Downs et al.,
"Google Scanned Objects: A High-Quality Dataset of 3D Scanned Household Items",
ICRA 2022, arXiv:2204.11918), licensed under CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), via the MuJoCo models by Kevin Zakka
(https://github.com/kevinzakka/mujoco_scanned_objects, commit
6ff8d275cebfd5b47e49685e3cfbe64b20e49a3c, MIT). The models are not redistributed in
this repository. They are fetched at run time, reduced to geometry, re-posed to a
stable resting pose and split into convex pieces for simulation. Per-object credits
are written with every selection (ATTRIBUTION.md next to selection.json).

From the v2 design space on, unbranded scans may also be published with the web app
as GLB files (web/public/assets/). These are adaptations under CC BY 4.0. Modified:
re-posed, split into convex pieces (CoACD, threshold 0.02, seed 0), simplified to 50 %,
texture coordinates flipped, re-encoded (meshopt geometry, WebP textures). Each such
asset carries its credit and its list of changes in the asset manifest, in every
replay that uses it, in docs/ATTRIBUTION.md and on the site's credits page.

